    "['binding tunnel [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `binding tunnel gre p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination dynamic\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel encapsulation gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 \"binding\" command for GRE P2MP like Huawei. Instead, we configure the tunnel parameters directly on the physical interface.\\n2. The \"p2mp\" aspect is implied by the \"tunnel destination dynamic\" in Juniper, which allows multiple destinations for this tunnel interface.\\n3. The IP address configuration is included as it\\'s typically part of the interface setup in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `binding tunnel gre p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination dynamic\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel encapsulation gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 \"binding\" command for GRE P2MP like Huawei. Instead, we configure the tunnel parameters directly on the physical interface.\\n2. The \"p2mp\" aspect is implied by the \"tunnel destination dynamic\" in Juniper, which allows multiple destinations for this tunnel interface.\\n3. The IP address configuration is included as it\\'s typically part of the interface setup in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination dynamic', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `binding tunnel gre p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination dynamic\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel encapsulation gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 \"binding\" command for GRE P2MP like Huawei. Instead, we configure the tunnel parameters directly on the physical interface.\\n2. The \"p2mp\" aspect is implied by the \"tunnel destination dynamic\" in Juniper, which allows multiple destinations for this tunnel interface.\\n3. The IP address configuration is included as it\\'s typically part of the interface setup in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination dynamic'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel encapsulation gre', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `binding tunnel gre p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination dynamic\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel encapsulation gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 \"binding\" command for GRE P2MP like Huawei. Instead, we configure the tunnel parameters directly on the physical interface.\\n2. The \"p2mp\" aspect is implied by the \"tunnel destination dynamic\" in Juniper, which allows multiple destinations for this tunnel interface.\\n3. The IP address configuration is included as it\\'s typically part of the interface setup in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel encapsulation gre'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel-protocol [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. Juniper uses `gr-` interface naming for GRE tunnels instead of `Tunnel`\\n2. The `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp` is split into two commands in Juniper:\\n   - `encapsulation gre` sets the GRE protocol\\n   - `multipoint` enables point-to-multipoint mode\\n3. Juniper requires specification of logical unit (typically unit 0) for tunnel interfaces\\n\\nNote: The actual interface name (gr-0/0/0) may vary depending on the Juniper platform and available interfaces.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. Juniper uses `gr-` interface naming for GRE tunnels instead of `Tunnel`\\n2. The `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp` is split into two commands in Juniper:\\n   - `encapsulation gre` sets the GRE protocol\\n   - `multipoint` enables point-to-multipoint mode\\n3. Juniper requires specification of logical unit (typically unit 0) for tunnel interfaces\\n\\nNote: The actual interface name (gr-0/0/0) may vary depending on the Juniper platform and available interfaces.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint'}]]": 1,
    "['source [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nOr if using a GRE interface in Juniper:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0 unit 0\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper typically uses \"gr-\" prefix for GRE interfaces (equivalent to Tunnel0) and \"ge-\" prefix for GigabitEthernet interfaces. The exact interface naming may vary based on Juniper platform.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0 unit 0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nOr if using a GRE interface in Juniper:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0 unit 0\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper typically uses \"gr-\" prefix for GRE interfaces (equivalent to Tunnel0) and \"ge-\" prefix for GigabitEthernet interfaces. The exact interface naming may vary based on Juniper platform.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0 unit 0'}]]": 1,
    "['ipsec profile [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set security ipsec profile <profile_name>', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset security ipsec profile <profile_name>\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the IPSec profile is referenced under the `st0` interface (similar to Huawei's Tunnel interface) using a similar syntax, but the actual profile definition would be configured separately under the `security ipsec` hierarchy. The above command shows how the profile is attached to the interface context.\", 'trans_template': 'set security ipsec profile <profile_name>'}]]": 1,
    "['ospf network-type [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0 interface <interface_name> interface-type p2mp', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent command for `ospf network-type p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ospf area 0 interface <interface_name> interface-type p2mp\\n##\\n\\nNote: In the Juniper command, you would replace `<interface_name>` with the actual interface name (e.g., `ge-0/0/0.0` or in this case likely the tunnel interface name). The Huawei command is applied under the interface configuration, while Juniper typically configures OSPF interface parameters under the protocols hierarchy.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0 interface <interface_name> interface-type p2mp'}]]": 1,
